   "html_text": "The above method of defining preference from a priority base presupposes complete information about whether an alternative possesses the properties in the base. In cases of incomplete information, beliefs play a crucial role, and agents’ preferences depend on them. This situation requires the introduction of formulas such as ⟦M⟧ ⟦M⟧ or ⟦M⟧ where ⟦M⟧ represents priorities. This approach enables complex aspects to be considered, e.g., determining whether certain properties from the priority base a",
   "md_text": "The above method of defining preference from a priority base presupposes complete information about whether an alternative possesses the properties in the base. In cases of incomplete information, beliefs play a crucial role, and agents’ preferences depend on them. This situation requires the introduction of formulas such as ⟦M⟧ ⟦M⟧ or ⟦M⟧ where ⟦M⟧ represents priorities. This approach enables complex aspects to be considered, e.g., determining whether certain properties from the priority base a"
