  {
   "i": 10,
   "shape_h": "p",
   "shape_m": "p",
   "html_text": "Pioneering logicians such as Halldén (1957) and von Wright (1963) proposed logics for preferences that focused on comparisons between situations. These logics extended propositional language with a binary connective, ⟦M⟧ , denoting the concept of preference or “betterness”.",
